    kalkDekningsbidragTitle:'Contribution margin',
    kalkDekningsbidragSubtitle:'See how much each unit you sell brings in after variable costs. This is called the contribution margin (CM). You also see how many you must sell to break even.',
    kalkDekningsbidragBackLabel:'Back to all tools',
    kalkDekningsbidragStatDb:'CM per unit',
    kalkDekningsbidragStatDg:'Contribution margin ratio',
    kalkDekningsbidragSectionInput:'Contribution margin',
    kalkDekningsbidragSectionHint:'Per unit + total',
    kalkDekningsbidragLblSalgspris:'Selling price per unit (kr)',
    kalkDekningsbidragLblVarkost:'Variable cost per unit (kr)',
    kalkDekningsbidragLblAntall:'Number of units sold',
    kalkDekningsbidragLblFixkost:'Fixed costs (kr)',
    kalkDekningsbidragWarn:'Variable cost exceeds the selling price — the product is not profitable.',
    kalkDekningsbidragInfoBox:'The contribution margin shows how much of the sales revenue is left to cover fixed costs and profit — after variable costs have been deducted. Break-even is the number of units you must sell for the total CM to cover all fixed costs.',
    kalkDekningsbidragResHeadline:'CM per unit',
    kalkDekningsbidragResDg:'Contribution margin ratio (CM%)',
    kalkDekningsbidragResTotalDb:'Total CM',
    kalkDekningsbidragResResultat:'Profit before tax',
    kalkDekningsbidragResBeEnheter:'Break-even (units)',
    kalkDekningsbidragResBeOms:'Break-even (revenue)',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoTitle:'How to use the Contribution Margin calculator',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow1Label:'1. Selling price and variable cost',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow1Desc:'The selling price is what you charge per unit. The variable cost is everything that varies with production — materials, ingredients, direct labour hours, packaging. CM per unit = selling price minus variable cost.',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow2Label:'2. Contribution margin ratio (CM%)',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow2Desc:'CM% = CM per unit / selling price × 100. A contribution margin ratio of 40 % means that 40 øre of every krone goes towards covering fixed costs and profit.',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow3Label:'3. Number of units and total CM',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow3Desc:'Total CM = CM per unit × number of units sold. This is the amount you have left after all variable costs, but before fixed costs.',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow4Label:'4. Fixed costs and profit',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow4Desc:'Fixed costs are independent of the quantity produced — rent, fixed salaries, insurance, leasing. Profit before tax = Total CM minus fixed costs.',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow5Label:'5. Break-even',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow5Desc:'Break-even quantity = fixed costs / CM per unit (rounded up). It is the number of units you MUST sell to break even. Break-even revenue = break-even quantity × selling price.',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow6Label:'6. Negative CM',
    kalkDekningsbidragHowtoRow6Desc:'If the variable cost is greater than the selling price, the CM is negative. You lose money on every sale — break-even is unattainable regardless of volume. In that case you must raise the price or reduce variable costs.',
