    kalkTimeprisResEffektiv:'Net per billed hour',
    kalkTimeprisDisclaimer:'Indicative calculation. The tax rate depends on total income, deductions and type of company. Contact an accountant for specific assessments.',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoTitle:'How to use the Hourly Rate calculator',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR1Title:'1. Set your net target',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR1Desc:'Enter what you want to be left with after tax per year — that is the basis for all calculations.',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR2Title:'2. Billable hours',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR2Desc:'Set realistic billable hours. 1 500 is common for consultants (40 h/week, 47 weeks, minus admin).',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR3Title:'3. Adjust the tax rate',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR3Desc:'30 % suits a sole proprietorship (ENK) with a middle income. If you earn more than around 700 000 kr, the rate is higher, up towards 35–40 %. See <a href="https://www.skatteetaten.no/satser/trinnskatt/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Skatteetaten\'s rates</a>.',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR4Title:'4. Sickness, pension and running costs',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR4Desc:'Holiday is already taken out of the billable hours. The surcharge for sickness and pension is a buffer for sick days and your own pension. Running costs of 15 % cover the accountant, equipment, insurance and courses.',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR5Title:'5. VAT (MVA) registration',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR5Desc:'Above 50 000 kr in revenue you must register for VAT (MVA). You then invoice the hourly rate plus 25 % VAT. The VAT is not your income. <a href="https://www.skatteetaten.no/bedrift-og-organisasjon/merverdiavgift/registrere-seg-i-mva-registeret/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read more at Skatteetaten.</a>',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR6Title:'6. Net per billed hour',
    kalkTimeprisHowtoR6Desc:'Your desired net divided by billable hours. It is what you keep per billed hour, after tax and costs.',
