    lonnTitle:'Salary after tax', lonnDesc:'Enter hourly wage and hours per week — see what you actually take home',
    lonnIntro:'Working part-time alongside school or studies? Enter your hourly wage and weekly hours to see gross pay, tax deductions, holiday pay, and your actual take-home pay. Based on Norwegian tax rules for 2026.',
    lonnLTimelonn:'Hourly wage (kr)', lonnLTimer:'Hours per week', lonnLUker:'Working weeks per year', lonnLAlder:'Age',
    lonnOptUnder18:'Under 18 years', lonnOpt18plus:'18 years or older',
    lonnFrikortHint:'The tax-free threshold for 2026 is 100,000 kr. If you earn less, no tax is deducted.',
    lonnBtnCalc:'Calculate pay →', lonnRLbl:'Take-home pay per month',
    lonnRlBruttoAar:'Gross annual pay', lonnRlBruttoMnd:'Gross monthly pay', lonnRlSkatt:'Tax deduction per year', lonnRlSkattMnd:'Tax deduction per month',
    lonnRlEffektiv:'Effective tax rate', lonnRlFeriepenger:'Holiday pay (10.2%)', lonnRlNettoAar:'Net annual pay (after tax)', lonnRlNettoTime:'Net per hour',
    lonnBdTitle:'Tax breakdown', lonnBdFrikort:'Below tax-free threshold — no tax', lonnBdTrinn:'Bracket tax', lonnBdAlm:'Ordinary income tax (22%)', lonnBdTrygd:'National insurance contribution', lonnBdMf:'Minimum deduction', lonnBdPf:'Personal allowance', lonnBdTotal:'Total tax',
    lonnVerdictFrikort:'You earn below the tax-free threshold — no tax!', lonnVerdictLav:'Low tax rate — typical for part-time work alongside studies.', lonnVerdictNormal:'Normal tax rate for your income level.',
    lonnDisclaimer:'* Simplified estimate. Actual tax deduction depends on your tax card. Holiday pay is normally paid out in June the following year.',
    lonnHowtoTitle:'How to use the Salary Calculator', lonnHowtoDesc:'Step-by-step guide for students',
    lonnHowtoRows:[['— HOW TO USE THE CALCULATOR —','Calculate what you actually take home from your part-time job'],['1. Hourly wage','Enter your hourly wage. Norway has no minimum wage, but typical rates for young workers are 160–220 kr.'],['2. Hours per week','How many hours do you work in a typical week? Part-time alongside school is usually 10–20 hours.'],['3. Working weeks per year','Standard is 47 weeks (52 minus 5 weeks holiday). If you only work during holidays, enter the number of weeks.'],['4. Age','Under 18: no national insurance contribution. Over 18: 7.6% national insurance contribution.'],['— HOW TO READ THE RESULTS —',''],['Tax-free card (100,000 kr)','If you earn less than 100,000 kr per year, no tax is deducted. You only need a frikort (order at skatteetaten.no).'],['Gross pay','What you earn BEFORE tax. Hourly wage × hours × weeks.'],['Tax deduction','What the government deducts in tax. Calculated from bracket tax, ordinary income tax and national insurance.'],['Holiday pay','Your employer sets aside 10.2% of your salary for holiday pay. Normally paid out in June the following year.'],['Net pay','What you actually receive in your account each month — after tax is deducted.'],['— GOOD TO KNOW —',''],['Tax card','Order your tax card at skatteetaten.no. Without a tax card, 50% tax is deducted!'],['Tax return','Even if you don\'t pay tax, you must check your tax return in April.'],['Holiday pay ≠ extra pay','Holiday pay replaces your salary during holidays — you receive it when you take time off.']],
