    bvlHowtoDesc: 'How to use Buy vs rent',
    bvlHowtoRows: [['— HOW TO USE THE CALCULATOR —','Compare total cost of owning vs renting over time'],['Purchase price','What the home costs to buy. Plus equity = home budget.'],['Equity','Share you pay yourself. The Lending Regulation requires min 10%.'],['Mortgage rate','Average rate over the loan period. Use today\'s rate if unsure.'],['Monthly rent','What a comparable home would cost to rent today.'],['Common costs','Monthly condo/HOA fees. Apartments typically 2,000-5,000 kr/month.'],['Maintenance','Annual upkeep as share of home value. Typically 1% (Norwegian standard).'],['Time horizon','How long will you live there? Shorter = renting often better. Longer = owning often better.'],['House-price growth','Expected annual growth. Norwegian historic average 1990-2024 is ~5%/year, but fluctuates.'],['Rent growth','Expected rent growth. Often 2-4%/year in big cities.'],['Alt. return','What your equity would earn in funds if you rented. Index funds average ~6-7%/year.'],['— HOW TO READ THE RESULTS —',''],['Net cost of buying','Interest + shared costs + maintenance − tax deduction − rise in value. Repayments don\'t count: they are your own money.'],['Net cost of renting','All rent over the period − what your equity could have earned in funds.'],['Break-even','The year buying becomes cheaper than renting and stays cheaper for the rest of the period.'],['Equity built by owning','Home value − remaining loan. What you\'re left with.'],['— GOOD TO KNOW —',''],['Short horizon','If you move within 5 years, buying often loses because of document duty and estate agent fees. These are not included here.'],['Long horizon','Over 15–20 years buying usually wins, because the rise in value has time to outweigh the costs.'],['Uncertain rate','Run the calculator with different rates — see how much it affects the result.']],
