    skattUttakInfoTitle: 'What is withdrawal taxation?',
    skattUttakInfoIntro: 'When you withdraw an asset, goods or services from the business for private use, it is treated for tax purposes as if you have sold it to yourself at market value. The gain is taxed under the normal rules.',
    skattUttakInfoFormulaLbl: 'Formula',
    skattUttakInfoFormula: 'Withdrawal gain = Market value − Tax-depreciated book value',
    skattUttakInfoEnkLbl: 'Sole trader (ENK)',
    skattUttakInfoEnkRow1: 'Tax: <b>Ordinary income 22 %</b>',
    skattUttakInfoEnkRow2: '+ National insurance <b>10.8 %</b> (with phase-in)',
    skattUttakInfoEnkRow3: '+ Bracket tax (if personal income)',
    skattUttakInfoEnkCond: 'Condition: cost price wholly/partly deducted (§ 5-2(1))',
    skattUttakInfoAsLbl: 'Limited company (AS)',
    skattUttakInfoAsRow1: 'Level 1: <b>Corporate tax 22 %</b>',
    skattUttakInfoAsRow2: 'Level 2: <b>Dividend tax ~37.84 %</b>',
    skattUttakInfoAsRow3: 'Gross-up: <b>×1.72</b>',
    skattUttakInfoAsCond: 'Withdrawal is deemed a dividend for the shareholder',
    skattUttakInfoExcLead: 'Exceptions and special rules',
    skattUttakInfoExc1: 'In an ENK, the withdrawal is only taxed if you have deducted the cost price, in full or in part (§ 5-2(1)).',
    skattUttakInfoExc2: 'If you give the business away and the recipient continues to run it, the withdrawal is not taxed (§ 9-7(4)).',
    skattUttakInfoExc3: 'If a company withdraws shares it owns in another company, the withdrawal may be tax-free for the company (the participation exemption, § 2-38).',
    skattUttakInfoExc4: 'If the withdrawal goes from a subsidiary to a shareholder, it is the subsidiary that is taxed for the withdrawal.',
    skattUttakInfoExc5: 'If you use the company\'s home, boat or car privately, the benefit is taxed to you: normally as a dividend, but as salary if you receive it as an employee (the shareholder model).',
    skattUttakInfoSource: 'Source: Tax Act § 5-2, § 5-3 and ch. 9. Indicative calculation.',
    skattUttakInfoDisclaimer: 'Simplified calculation. Bracket tax 2026: bracket 1 (1.7 %), 2 (4.0 %), 3 (13.7 %), 4 (16.8 %), 5 (17.8 %). National insurance with lower threshold 99 650 kr and phase-in rule 25 %.',
