    kalkNetthandelLblCacCap: '(kr)',
    kalkNetthandelResHeadline: 'Result',
    kalkNetthandelMinusVare: '− Cost of goods',
    kalkNetthandelMinusFrakt: '− Shipping',
    kalkNetthandelMinusGebyr: '− Payment fee',
    kalkNetthandelMinusEmb: '− Packaging',
    kalkNetthandelMndDb: 'That is also the most you can spend on ads per order (break-even CPA).',
    kalkNetthandelMndMinus: 'The order loses money before any ad costs. Raise the price or cut variable costs.',
    kalkNetthandelMndEmptyOrdre: 'Enter the average order to see the result.',
    kalkNetthandelMndEmptySaas: 'Enter the monthly churn to see the result.',
    kalkNetthandelMndCac: 'Enter the cost per new customer to compare.',
    kalkNetthandelMndSunt: 'A customer is worth {x} times what it costs to win them. 3 times or more is considered healthy.',
    kalkNetthandelMndLav: 'A customer is worth {x} times what it costs to win them. Below 3 times, you are spending a lot to win customers.',
    kalkNetthandelMndTap: 'A customer is worth less than it costs to win them. Every new customer loses you money.',
    kalkNetthandelResCpaFull: 'Break-even CPA (max ad cost/order)',
    kalkNetthandelResGross: 'Gross margin per customer',
    kalkNetthandelNoteOrdre: 'All amounts are excl. VAT.',
    kalkNetthandelNoteSaas: 'All amounts are excl. VAT. Customer value assumes churn and margin stay the same.',
    kalkNetthandelFormelToggle: 'Show formula',
    kalkNetthandelF1: 'CM per order = AOV − variable costs · Contribution margin ratio = CM / AOV',
    kalkNetthandelF2: 'Break-even ROAS = 1 / Contribution margin ratio · Break-even CPA = AOV × Contribution margin ratio',
    kalkNetthandelF3: 'LTV = (ARPU × Gross margin%) / Churn · Lifetime = 1 / Churn',
    kalkNetthandelF4: 'LTV:CAC = LTV / CAC · CAC payback = CAC / (ARPU × Gross margin%)',
    kalkNetthandelFNote: '“A ROAS of 1.93 means every krone spent on ads must return at least 1.93 kr in sales to break even. LTV:CAC ≥ 3 is considered healthy.”',
    kalkNetthandelGuideKicker: 'How to calculate',
    kalkNetthandelGuideTitle: 'From order to customer value',
    kalkNetthandelStep1: '<b>Per order — do you make money on the sale?</b> Subtract cost of goods, shipping, payment fees and packaging from the average order. What is left is the contribution margin per order.',
    kalkNetthandelStep2: '<b>How much can you pay for the sale?</b> With a contribution margin ratio of 51.7 %, an order of 600 kr can cost up to 310 kr in ads (break-even CPA). Each ad krone must then bring in at least 1.93 kr in sales (break-even ROAS).',
    kalkNetthandelStep3: '<b>Subscription — what is a customer worth?</b> If 2.5 % of customers leave each month, a customer stays 40 months on average. With 400 kr in gross margin per month, the customer is worth 16 000 kr (LTV). Compare this with what it costs to win a new customer (CAC).',
    kalkNetthandelStripRoas: 'Minimum sales per ad krone (ROAS)',
    kalkNetthandelStripCpa: 'Max ad cost per order (CPA)',
    kalkNetthandelStripRatio: 'Customer value vs. cost (LTV:CAC)',
    kalkNetthandelStripPayback: 'Time to earn back the customer',
    kalkNetthandelTableTitle: 'Both examples step by step',
    kalkNetthandelTblOrdreH: 'Per order',
    kalkNetthandelTblVariable: 'Variable costs',
    kalkNetthandelTblSaasH: 'Subscription',
    kalkNetthandelWhoKicker: 'Who uses it',
    kalkNetthandelWhoTitle: 'Three typical cases',
    kalkNetthandelWho1Lbl: 'Online store · advertising',
    kalkNetthandelWho1Desc: 'See how much ad spend an order can carry (CPA) and how much each ad krone must sell (ROAS).',
    kalkNetthandelWho2Lbl: 'SaaS · growth',
    kalkNetthandelWho2Desc: 'LTV:CAC and payback decide how aggressively you can buy new customers without draining your cash reserves.',
    kalkNetthandelWho3Lbl: 'Subscription box',
    kalkNetthandelWho3Desc: 'Treat each box as an order, and the customer as a subscription with churn.',
    kalkNetthandelFaqQ1: 'What is break-even ROAS?',
    kalkNetthandelFaqA1: 'The lowest return on ad spend at which an order exactly breaks even. With a contribution margin ratio of 51.7 %, break-even ROAS is 1.93 — every krone spent on ads must return at least 1.93 kr in sales. Above that, your advertising makes money.',
    kalkNetthandelFaqQ2: 'What is a healthy LTV:CAC ratio?',
    kalkNetthandelFaqA2: 'The rule of thumb is that LTV should be at least 3 times CAC. Below 3:1 you are spending too much to acquire customers; far above may mean you are underinvesting in growth. The example lands at 6.4:1.',
    kalkNetthandelFaqQ3: 'Are the figures calculated with or without VAT?',
    kalkNetthandelFaqA3: 'Excl. VAT. Use average order and monthly revenue excl. VAT, otherwise the contribution margin ratio and customer value come out too high. For a VAT-registered business, VAT only passes through the till and is not income.',
    kalkNetthandelRel1Desc: 'Set the right price from cost of goods, and see the difference between markup and the contribution margin ratio.',
    kalkNetthandelRel2Desc: 'Cost per unit — even when the variants are not equally demanding.',
    kalkNetthandelRel3Desc: 'Full costing from materials to price, with surcharges and profit.',
    kalkTimeprisModusTitle: 'Mode',
